      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX 3 Image Klein edit\n\nThe fast, editing-first FLUX 3 model, with the three dials FLUX 3 Image does not have: `seed`, `steps` and `output_format`.\n\n`seed` is **42**, **fixed**, so the same input and prompt give the same image. Set it to **-1** for a fresh random seed each run.\n\n`steps` is **16**, the maximum and the default. Fewer is faster and rougher.\n\n`resolution` is **default**, which leaves it out of the request: an edit then comes back at the input's own size, a text-to-image at 1k. There is no `match_input` on Klein because that is already what it does. Exact `width` / `height` start at 64 here rather than 256.\n\nThe API runs Klein's prompt upsampler for you, so a short instruction is fine; `expanded_prompt` shows the caption it wrote. Klein has no `grounding` or `version`.\n\nDisconnect the image and the same node does text-to-image. Up to 10 references, as on FLUX 3 Image.\n\n## The prompt lives in one node\n\nThe **Shared Prompt** node feeds the prompt in this graph, so there is one\nplace to edit it. It emits a plain string, **not** a list. That is the difference between it and **Prompt\nList**, which would make each node it feeds run once per line and multiply what the graph\ncosts."
      ],
      "title": "Read me",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
